bcon: anchor C=1 image placements to the text, like kitty

C=1 placements used a screen-relative row, so they did not scroll with the
text and survived a screen clear: an image placed near the bottom (e.g. by
`kitten icat`, which places with C=1 and prints the newlines itself) stayed
pinned over the prompt. They now use an absolute row, scroll/prune with the
text and are deleted by ED 2/3. Text writes still do not remove them.
